# Per-Dockerfile ignore: excludes everything, then whitelists the bits this
# Dockerfile actually copies. The JVM service images have their own, next to
# infra/docker/service/Dockerfile.
*

# Yarn workspace root manifests. Yarn validates the whole workspace
# graph at install time, so every workspace member's package.json
# must be present even though only console + ui source
# gets COPY-ed below: a member missing here is a lockfile
# `--immutable` refuses. The js CI job checks each member the root
# package.json lists is admitted here and copied by the Dockerfile.
!package.json
!yarn.lock
!.yarnrc.yml
!bases/console
!bases/demo-digital-bank-app/package.json
!components/ui
!infra/docker/console

# Landing.svelte ?raw-imports a handful of ADRs, TDDs, and recipes
# via `../../../../docs/...`. Whitelist just those three subtrees so
# the build context stays small (docs/slides is ~500MB locally with
# its node_modules cache, and docs/prd / docs/plan aren't referenced).
!docs/adr
!docs/tdd
!docs/recipes

# Re-exclude per-brick build artefacts inside the whitelisted dirs.
# Yarn 4 hoists node_modules to the workspace root, but stray
# per-brick caches from a host `yarn dev` session can still appear.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.svelte-kit
**/.vite
**/*.log
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz
